{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Aaron took Elisheva daughter of Amminadav, sister of Nahshon.</b> This verse informs us that the family of the priesthood merged with the family of royalty — she is Elisheva, sister of Nahshon, the great prince of Israel. And Scripture mentions the mother of Pinhas, who is also a priest who acquired his portion through himself; and so is the way of Scripture with the kings of the land, that it mentions them by the name of their mother, in the manner of what is written (I Kings 15:2): ״ושם אמו מעכה בת אבישלום״, and (II Chronicles 13:2) ״ושם אמו עזובה בת שלחי״. And it says ״מבנות פוטיאל״ — he is Yitro, or Yosef — and did not say בת פוטיאל, because Putiel had many daughters and he took one of them." "<b>And behold</b> in this parashah you will find six prophets who are from the tribe of Levi, and they are: Aharon, Moshe, Pinhas (who is Eliyahu), and the three sons of Korah — Asir, Elkanah, and Aviasaf — for so the Rabbis of blessed memory counted them among the 48 prophets. And these six were in a single generation. And perhaps these three sons of Korah are those of whom Scripture says (Numbers 26:11): ״ובני קרח לא מתו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Source cites דברי הימים ב כ לא for the Azuvah citation; normalized to II Chronicles 13:2, the verse actually containing that phrase."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:33.950255673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}